# How a merge between two machines' vaults resolves, by file class (orient plan
# multi-machine-safe-durable-data-locally, Decisions). Union is only for files that are
# append-only by design; a structured file (JSON, YAML, plans, tables) must never be unioned.

# Append-only logs: keep both sides' new lines. Records under <host>/ have one writer and
# never merge in practice; union is the safety net.
*.jsonl merge=union
Engineering/*/ledger.md merge=union
Engineering/*/ideas-log.md merge=union
Customers/*/ledger.md merge=union

# Derived indexes: keep ours and regenerate (wp index / cust) after the pull.
# Needs `git config merge.ours.driver true` in each clone.
Engineering/index.md merge=ours
Customers/index.md merge=ours

# One writer machine (config.yaml manifestWriter); never merge it, take one side whole.
.knowledge/manifest.json -merge
